WEBVTT

00:00:05.419 --> 00:00:08.320
The Irresponsible Captain
Tylor

00:00:09.023 --> 00:00:11.892
We may be off the maps...
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:11.892 --> 00:00:13.951
...but let's stay on this voyage.
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:14.795 --> 00:00:18.925
I will be holding, never let you go.

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:23.337
Whatever we may want...
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:23.337 --> 00:00:25.464
...we'll take as we need.
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.267
So let's just go wherever we please!
Omoi no Mama Yukou!

00:00:31.979 --> 00:00:34.749
Make me your partner...
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:34.749 --> 00:00:37.377
...on this journey.
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:37.651 --> 00:00:41.246
One that you trust more than words!
Michizure ni Shite

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:47.354
Come on now and sail away for future!
Imasugu sail away for future

00:00:48.362 --> 00:00:49.864
Things are waiting...
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:49.864 --> 00:00:53.061
...that we've never seen before!
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:54.902 --> 00:00:57.071
Just take your cares...
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:00:57.071 --> 00:01:01.132
...and throw them all away.
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:01:01.375 --> 00:01:06.005
Come together, just think of tomorrow.

00:01:07.782 --> 00:01:09.272
Let's go!

00:01:12.653 --> 00:01:15.952
ENEMY! CRISIS!
WE SURRENDER!

00:01:24.331 --> 00:01:28.461
So, the captain and the first
officer are still kicking, huh?

00:01:29.703 --> 00:01:32.035
Then it's time
for the final option.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:36.369
Captain! If you don't rescind
that irresponsible order soon...

00:01:36.444 --> 00:01:37.843
...all hell will break loose!

00:01:38.813 --> 00:01:40.804
Did I say something wrong?

00:01:41.782 --> 00:01:46.879
Did you not tell those ruffians
to do whatever they want to?!

00:01:47.455 --> 00:01:50.219
Oh. I did, didn't I?

00:01:52.126 --> 00:01:52.990
Captain!

00:01:53.461 --> 00:01:56.589
If they do whatever they want,
there's no telling what will happen!

00:01:57.631 --> 00:02:00.259
Sir, I request that you
rescind the order at once!

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:01.360
Denied.

00:02:04.805 --> 00:02:08.673
Then at least order them
not to fight in the hangar!

00:02:08.742 --> 00:02:09.731
Also denied.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:10.277
Then...

00:02:10.277 --> 00:02:11.175
Denied!

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.839
Man, it's good
to be the captain!

00:02:15.116 --> 00:02:18.051
I hope you get promoted
someday soon, Mr. Yamamoto.

00:02:19.687 --> 00:02:21.622
Of course.
The first officer...

00:02:21.622 --> 00:02:24.614
...can't countermand the
captain's orders, can he?

00:02:25.159 --> 00:02:28.026
Mr. Tylor is
Mr. Yamamoto's superior.

00:02:28.162 --> 00:02:31.290
Mr. Yamamoto is
Mr. Tylor's subordinate.

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:36.568
He still doesn't understand
how bad this ship really is.

00:02:37.138 --> 00:02:40.107
How no new captain ever
lasts more than three days...

00:02:40.307 --> 00:02:43.435
...and how it's considered the
dumping ground of the UPSF.

00:02:56.357 --> 00:02:59.884
Damn it! I can't cut loose
with my feet on the ground!

00:03:04.431 --> 00:03:05.329
Come back here!

00:03:08.869 --> 00:03:12.930
The traditional battle between the
Marines and the pilots is over.

00:03:13.674 --> 00:03:16.438
Now the really fun show begins!

00:03:21.382 --> 00:03:23.009
"Fun show?"

00:03:32.893 --> 00:03:33.951
A coup d'etat?!

00:03:34.161 --> 00:03:38.495
Yes, sir! Your thoughtless
and irresponsible orders...

00:03:38.599 --> 00:03:41.261
...have driven the
veterans to mutiny!

00:03:44.872 --> 00:03:47.864
This must be the "fun show"
Cryburn was talking about.

00:03:48.242 --> 00:03:49.231
What'll we do?

00:03:49.543 --> 00:03:51.670
I don't know, either!

00:03:51.912 --> 00:03:54.472
Tylor told them to do
whatever they wanted to...

00:03:54.548 --> 00:03:56.516
...so they really
started doing it.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:59.216
What do you intend
to do, Captain?

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:04.254
Sounds like fun. Let's see
if we can join the coup.

00:04:04.758 --> 00:04:09.525
Captain Tylor, they're
mutinying against YOU!

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.830
You're their enemy!

00:04:12.533 --> 00:04:15.730
Enemy? I'm no enemy.

00:04:16.437 --> 00:04:21.568
Captain! It's that irresponsible
attitude that's caused this!

00:04:28.849 --> 00:04:32.808
Go! Seize the bridge
and the ship is ours!

00:04:39.927 --> 00:04:41.895
I didn't expect to run
out of pain killers...

00:04:41.962 --> 00:04:44.522
...before even getting
to the battle zone.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:56.337
This calls for
old-fashioned methods.

00:05:08.956 --> 00:05:10.947
Nah, it'd be a waste.

00:05:11.625 --> 00:05:12.489
Captain!

00:05:13.627 --> 00:05:15.729
I suggest you order the
issue of Class One armament...

00:05:15.729 --> 00:05:17.253
...to the bridge personnel!

00:05:18.132 --> 00:05:20.362
And what exactly is
Class One armament?

00:05:21.902 --> 00:05:24.632
In any case,
we have to fight them!

00:05:25.005 --> 00:05:26.700
To maintain military discipline!

00:05:29.143 --> 00:05:29.939
Wait!

00:05:31.312 --> 00:05:32.210
Commander Star!

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:37.617
No, we can't! Fellow UPSF
soldiers mustn't fight each other!

00:05:38.319 --> 00:05:40.913
We have to try and settle
this through discussion.

00:05:41.355 --> 00:05:43.653
These aren't people
you can reason with!

00:05:43.857 --> 00:05:47.349
No, if we try to
understand each other...

00:05:47.761 --> 00:05:49.956
...we can settle
this peacefully!

00:05:53.901 --> 00:05:55.368
Cmdr. Yuriko Star!

00:05:55.669 --> 00:05:59.298
I love how you throw your
heart into your work!

00:06:00.708 --> 00:06:03.477
The fact that I can sail
on the same ship with you...

00:06:03.477 --> 00:06:05.809
...truly makes me the
happiest man in space!

00:06:07.781 --> 00:06:12.775
Ow! All I did was hold
your hand! That's really cold.

00:06:12.986 --> 00:06:15.978
Captain Tylor, you are unfit
to be called captain...

00:06:16.123 --> 00:06:18.557
No! You're unfit to be
called a human being!

00:06:23.731 --> 00:06:26.564
Captain, I've a message
from Lieutenant Andressen.

00:06:29.069 --> 00:06:30.366
Putting it on the monitor.

00:06:30.738 --> 00:06:31.898
Right. Please do.

00:06:35.209 --> 00:06:37.734
How's it going, Captain?

00:06:38.145 --> 00:06:40.670
We'll be paying you
a visit, soon.

00:06:40.781 --> 00:06:44.182
Why don't you spare yourself
the pain and surrender now?

00:06:44.785 --> 00:06:48.414
Surrender? That might
be a good idea, too.

00:06:48.722 --> 00:06:49.654
Captain!

00:06:51.158 --> 00:06:53.927
Men, listen to me!
I understand perfectly...

00:06:53.927 --> 00:06:56.657
...how disgruntled you are with
the captain's incompetence...

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:59.494
...and that it's
driven you to mutiny!

00:07:01.101 --> 00:07:04.036
But you're violating
military discipline!

00:07:05.005 --> 00:07:06.973
Discipline is
everything for a soldier!

00:07:07.174 --> 00:07:10.439
Now obey regulations, throw down
your weapons, and surrender.

00:07:12.079 --> 00:07:14.206
Discipline?
Don't make me laugh!

00:07:14.715 --> 00:07:16.046
Discipline doesn't win a war!

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.652
What you need
in war is strength!

00:07:18.652 --> 00:07:22.713
Strength's all that
lets you survive and win!

00:07:23.123 --> 00:07:24.249
That's not true!

00:07:24.858 --> 00:07:26.519
What you need in war...

00:07:27.127 --> 00:07:28.321
...is love!

00:07:30.264 --> 00:07:33.756
If we love each other
and fight as one...

00:07:34.067 --> 00:07:36.092
...then we may be able
to beat the Raalgon!

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:38.763
Please, put your weapons down!

00:07:39.106 --> 00:07:41.802
Trying to talk us out
of this? I love it!

00:07:47.581 --> 00:07:51.574
They shouldn't take this so
seriously. It's just a war.

00:08:00.928 --> 00:08:04.227
Uh, Mr. Yamamoto,
how do I use this?

00:08:05.232 --> 00:08:05.891
Here they come!

00:08:16.176 --> 00:08:16.767
Get down!

00:08:37.798 --> 00:08:38.628
Now what?

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:49.631
We're warping!
Shut it down, fast!

00:08:53.146 --> 00:08:54.704
I can't! It's too late!

00:08:55.148 --> 00:08:56.240
Target coordinates?!

00:08:56.483 --> 00:08:57.973
That's the problem!
I didn't enter any!

00:09:01.455 --> 00:09:02.979
A random warp...

00:09:03.824 --> 00:09:05.917
We don't know where
we'll materialize.

00:09:06.059 --> 00:09:11.361
If it's in a city on some
planet, then millions...

00:09:11.899 --> 00:09:14.026
No, BILLIONS of people may die!

00:09:14.401 --> 00:09:17.632
Why are you always
so pessimistic?

00:09:18.338 --> 00:09:22.798
We might come out near a planet
with nice weather, good food...

00:09:22.876 --> 00:09:25.208
...and tons of pretty girls!

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:27.915
Captain! You are!

00:09:27.915 --> 00:09:28.549
Warp entry in fifteen seconds!
Captain! You are!

00:09:28.549 --> 00:09:29.607
Warp entry in fifteen seconds!

00:09:30.317 --> 00:09:32.785
All hands, brace for
dimensional-shift shock!

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:05.750
We're... We're okay.

00:10:06.286 --> 00:10:11.121
You see? Things don't
always turn out bad.

00:10:12.125 --> 00:10:14.457
Captain! I'm picking
up an energy source!

00:10:14.962 --> 00:10:16.122
Putting it on the monitor!

00:10:19.266 --> 00:10:19.925
Oh, my.

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:21.867
A Raalgon fleet!

00:10:31.645 --> 00:10:33.044
Prepare to open fire!

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:38.178
Evasive action impossible!

00:10:38.652 --> 00:10:40.779
Sending SOS on
the emergency channel!

00:10:40.887 --> 00:10:41.945
We're doomed!

00:10:42.122 --> 00:10:43.453
Father!

00:10:45.525 --> 00:10:47.322
What do we do, Captain?!

00:10:47.995 --> 00:10:48.825
Captain!

00:10:52.633 --> 00:10:53.395
Captain!

00:11:01.008 --> 00:11:02.839
That's a good question.

00:11:30.037 --> 00:11:31.061
Where do you
think you're going?

00:11:31.238 --> 00:11:32.865
I'm not gonna die like this!

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:36.134
If I have to go, it's gonna
be in my plane's cockpit!

00:11:36.376 --> 00:11:40.608
We gonna let the flyboy
get all the glory, Skipper?

00:11:42.349 --> 00:11:43.873
Let's charge
those enemy ships!

00:11:45.619 --> 00:11:47.484
Fighting each other
only moments ago...

00:11:48.088 --> 00:11:50.955
...but now united in the
face of the true enemy!

00:11:51.358 --> 00:11:55.294
This is how true UPSF
soldiers SHOULD behave!

00:11:58.198 --> 00:11:59.665
Everyone, listen to me!

00:12:00.767 --> 00:12:03.167
That we will die
here is certain!

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:06.104
But our deaths will
not be in vain!

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:10.744
It will go down in history that
the destroyer Soyokaze...

00:12:10.744 --> 00:12:14.305
...was the first vessel to
fire upon the Raalgon Empire!

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:17.542
Let's surrender!

00:12:25.425 --> 00:12:29.156
Ca... Captain...
What did you just?

00:12:30.363 --> 00:12:31.625
We're going to surrender.

00:12:32.099 --> 00:12:34.401
If we open fire,
we're just going to die.

00:12:34.401 --> 00:12:36.460
But... But, sir!

00:12:36.703 --> 00:12:39.194
What about the pride of the
United Planets Space Force?

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:41.703
Who cares about pride?

00:12:41.808 --> 00:12:44.208
Dying won't be very fun,
so let's surrender.

00:12:45.679 --> 00:12:49.342
Captain, do you have
some sort of plan?

00:12:50.484 --> 00:12:51.883
Things will work out.

00:12:57.057 --> 00:13:00.959
Lt. Kyon-Hwa Kim! Please signal
our surrender to the enemy ship.

00:13:04.464 --> 00:13:05.522
Aye, aye, sir.

00:13:07.934 --> 00:13:10.596
How can he be so calm in
the face of an enemy fleet?

00:13:11.938 --> 00:13:15.066
He must have some
sort of plan.

00:13:18.145 --> 00:13:19.908
Unconditional surrender?

00:13:20.147 --> 00:13:22.911
Aye, sir. We just
received their signal.

00:13:23.483 --> 00:13:25.007
Surrender...

00:13:25.619 --> 00:13:29.316
Unfathomable for us. It is
a uniquely human concept.

00:13:30.791 --> 00:13:35.728
Hold fire. Signal the enemy vessel
that we accept their surrender.

00:13:36.062 --> 00:13:37.654
But... But, Captain!

00:13:38.165 --> 00:13:41.430
There's no profit in destroying
one broken-down old ship.

00:13:41.868 --> 00:13:45.634
But it could be a source
of useful information.

00:13:46.006 --> 00:13:47.030
I see.

00:13:48.675 --> 00:13:51.769
Link the fire control systems
of our other ships to this one...

00:13:52.179 --> 00:13:56.172
...and program them
to fire when we do!

00:14:02.155 --> 00:14:05.124
Okay, everyone.
Be on your best behavior.

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:32.075
I see. Now I understand why this
scrap heap is in the battle zone.

00:14:32.485 --> 00:14:35.147
You had a mutiny here,
didn't you?

00:14:35.522 --> 00:14:37.649
Wow, how'd you know?

00:14:38.525 --> 00:14:40.891
You Raalgon captains
are really smart!

00:14:41.428 --> 00:14:43.896
I've no desire to talk with
an underling like you!

00:14:44.531 --> 00:14:45.725
Who's the captain here?!

00:14:46.233 --> 00:14:47.564
That's me!

00:14:48.368 --> 00:14:49.858
YOU'RE the captain?!

00:14:51.438 --> 00:14:55.272
Uh-huh. Since we're both
captains, let's be friends.

00:14:56.543 --> 00:14:58.511
You little!

00:14:58.912 --> 00:15:03.008
You dare mock the proud
soldiers of the Raalgon Empire?!

00:15:03.516 --> 00:15:06.747
That really wasn't
my intention, sir!

00:15:07.254 --> 00:15:09.723
Those who renounce war must
obey without question!

00:15:09.723 --> 00:15:12.157
That is common
sense to we Raalgon!

00:15:13.126 --> 00:15:18.063
Now give us the UPSF's
operation orders!

00:15:18.598 --> 00:15:22.034
If we give you that, our main
fleet will be destroyed!

00:15:22.569 --> 00:15:23.399
Damn it all!

00:15:24.104 --> 00:15:25.867
Prepare it for us at once!

00:15:26.873 --> 00:15:30.274
Can't... breathe...
Okay! Just let me go!

00:15:30.677 --> 00:15:32.736
Now printing
document.
Please wait
a moment.

00:15:40.787 --> 00:15:45.019
To think they'd learn the location
of our main fleet like this!

00:15:46.192 --> 00:15:48.888
All that's left now is for
me to sacrifice my life!

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:51.989
If you're gonna try it,
wait till they're leaving.

00:15:52.399 --> 00:15:53.229
Andressen!

00:15:53.934 --> 00:15:56.425
They're gonna waste us the
minute they're done here.

00:15:57.570 --> 00:15:59.470
I'm in with you guys.

00:16:00.006 --> 00:16:02.600
If you gotta die, you may
as well have lots of company.

00:16:02.809 --> 00:16:03.673
Men!

00:16:09.316 --> 00:16:13.776
We Raalgon are
a race born to fight.

00:16:13.954 --> 00:16:16.582
We never surrender or
retreat like you people.

00:16:17.157 --> 00:16:20.991
Victory or death are
the only paths we follow!

00:16:21.161 --> 00:16:22.093
I see.

00:16:22.629 --> 00:16:26.065
Do you know what concepts
are required for victory?

00:16:26.333 --> 00:16:27.891
No. What are they?

00:16:28.168 --> 00:16:32.832
What lead to victory are love,
strength, and discipline.

00:16:33.139 --> 00:16:36.042
Love of country, possession
of great military strength...

00:16:36.042 --> 00:16:38.178
...and the discipline to
control that strength.

00:16:38.178 --> 00:16:40.880
You must start with those
in order to ensure victory.

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:43.610
Wow, you Raalgon Empire
guys are really smart!

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:48.484
Everyone here has their own
ideas and can never agree.

00:16:48.755 --> 00:16:49.380
Right?

00:16:49.689 --> 00:16:52.325
If you humans can't
control a single ship...

00:16:52.325 --> 00:16:55.021
...then there's no way you
can defeat the Raalgon Empire.

00:16:55.628 --> 00:16:57.596
Maybe you're right.

00:16:59.933 --> 00:17:01.161
Thank you
for waiting.

00:17:06.439 --> 00:17:07.872
Our business here is finished.

00:17:13.079 --> 00:17:13.670
Now!

00:17:15.949 --> 00:17:16.540
Hold it!

00:17:17.317 --> 00:17:18.147
Look!

00:17:19.319 --> 00:17:20.047
That's!

00:17:25.258 --> 00:17:26.919
Please, accept this gift.

00:17:27.727 --> 00:17:28.716
Gift?

00:17:29.029 --> 00:17:32.863
Yes, as thanks for
teaching us so much.

00:17:33.633 --> 00:17:35.969
After all, we got to
hear a live talk from...

00:17:35.969 --> 00:17:39.166
...a professional
Raalgon imperial soldier!

00:17:39.806 --> 00:17:43.867
We're grateful to have
received such valuable advice.

00:17:44.944 --> 00:17:46.411
What is your name?

00:17:47.447 --> 00:17:49.506
Justy Ueki Tylor, age twenty.

00:17:49.682 --> 00:17:52.378
That name shall be
entered in the record.

00:17:54.487 --> 00:17:55.852
Entered in the record?

00:17:56.423 --> 00:17:58.414
Oh, don't go to any
trouble on my account!

00:17:58.925 --> 00:18:00.859
That's... Isn't that?!

00:18:01.094 --> 00:18:01.924
Yeah...

00:18:03.696 --> 00:18:07.427
Did the captain surrender because
he planned this from the start?

00:18:08.334 --> 00:18:10.598
No... I don't believe it!

00:18:14.207 --> 00:18:17.768
Once we're back on board,
open fire!

00:18:17.977 --> 00:18:18.534
Aye, sir!

00:18:19.779 --> 00:18:21.347
Poor fool.

00:18:21.347 --> 00:18:24.976
Giving me a present without
knowing his ultimate fate.

00:18:25.652 --> 00:18:28.088
Now that we know the
position of their main fleet...

00:18:28.088 --> 00:18:31.421
...the Raalgon Empire is
sure to win this war!

00:18:36.096 --> 00:18:37.586
Huh? What's wrong?

00:18:46.306 --> 00:18:48.467
Malfunction in the
fire control system!

00:18:49.142 --> 00:18:50.973
Auto-fire cannot
be disengaged!

00:18:58.384 --> 00:19:00.477
Mr. Katori!
Get us out of here!

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:01.718
Aye, aye!

00:19:11.164 --> 00:19:15.100
Relax! As long as I'm at
the helm, we'll be fine!

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:34.413
Captain, did you surrender
to trick the enemy?!

00:19:35.021 --> 00:19:36.852
Victory through brainpower, huh?

00:19:37.924 --> 00:19:40.222
You guessed what
was in our present.

00:19:40.527 --> 00:19:42.324
You're a helluva
captain, sir!

00:19:42.862 --> 00:19:46.798
Even I wasn't able to guess
there was a bomb inside!

00:19:47.066 --> 00:19:49.660
What? That was a bomb?

00:19:51.604 --> 00:19:55.506
Oh, it was a bomb!
I didn't realize.

00:19:56.643 --> 00:19:59.979
Captain! Do you mean to say
you were ready to give away...

00:19:59.979 --> 00:20:03.073
...our military secrets to
the enemy to save yourself?!

00:20:03.149 --> 00:20:06.550
I feel sorry for him.
That poor captain...

00:20:10.757 --> 00:20:14.961
Dom, answer me. Is it true
that our reconnaissance fleet...

00:20:14.961 --> 00:20:17.020
...was defeated by
a single destroyer?

00:20:17.630 --> 00:20:19.325
It is the truth, Highness.

00:20:19.632 --> 00:20:23.432
I see...
Dom, I appreciate your candor.

00:20:24.103 --> 00:20:26.469
Wang and the others
never tell me the truth.

00:20:27.373 --> 00:20:29.466
The enemy destroyer
was the Soyokaze.

00:20:29.876 --> 00:20:33.505
Its captain is named
Justy Ueki Tylor.

00:20:35.515 --> 00:20:36.880
Tylor...

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:42.747
Have him brought before me!

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:45.217
What do you mean?

00:20:46.392 --> 00:20:49.293
I wish to meet this
man "Tylor" in person.

00:20:50.797 --> 00:20:54.198
I've been having
similar thoughts, Highness.

00:20:54.367 --> 00:20:57.530
I see.
Then go to it at once.

00:20:57.971 --> 00:20:58.665
As you wish.

00:21:00.773 --> 00:21:01.899
By the way, Dom...

00:21:02.375 --> 00:21:03.171
Yes, Highness?

00:21:03.776 --> 00:21:06.643
I'd like to
ask you something.

00:21:07.814 --> 00:21:10.044
What must one
do to win a war?

00:21:11.751 --> 00:21:15.414
You mean what is most needed
to win a war, Highness?

00:21:18.658 --> 00:21:20.216
That would be luck.

00:21:20.426 --> 00:21:24.385
I believe good fortune
in war is most important.

00:21:25.331 --> 00:21:26.457
Good fortune?

00:21:26.532 --> 00:21:27.157
Yes.

00:21:28.668 --> 00:21:31.899
Then I wish good
fortune for you, Dom.

00:21:36.075 --> 00:21:37.303
Tylor...

00:21:37.977 --> 00:21:41.276
I look forward to the day
we meet on the battlefield.

00:21:52.091 --> 00:21:56.118
This is Lt. Cmdr. Justy Ueki Tylor,
captain of the destroyer Soyokaze!

00:21:56.262 --> 00:21:58.560
We have destroyed
four enemy ships!

00:21:58.631 --> 00:22:01.828
I repeat, we have destroyed
four enemy ships!

00:22:12.478 --> 00:22:13.410
The Irresponsible Captain Tylor
Next Episode

00:22:15.548 --> 00:22:18.351
If I should die in this war,
at least let there be...

00:22:18.351 --> 00:22:21.479
...a lovely angel in white
caring for me at the end.

00:22:21.654 --> 00:22:25.249
Next time, "'Angel in White'
Begins With an H." Watch for it.

00:22:25.358 --> 00:22:27.189
Filming is Job 1!
Working hard for those who demand
the finest in image and sound

00:22:38.338 --> 00:22:41.441
All he has to do is just...
Machi o Aitsu ga Aruiteru dake de

00:22:41.441 --> 00:22:44.535
...walk around downtown.
Machi o Aitsu ga Aruiteru dake de

00:22:45.044 --> 00:22:48.514
He's a playful man who catches...
Nandemo Ki o Hiku Ochame na Yatsu sa

00:22:48.514 --> 00:22:51.347
...the eyes of all who he meets.
Nandemo Ki o Hiku Ochame na Yatsu sa

00:22:51.851 --> 00:22:54.687
Oh! That's why, you see...
Aa, Dakara sa Sou Kore kara Shuyaku

00:22:54.687 --> 00:22:58.487
...he'll be our hero from now on.
Aa, Dakara sa Sou Kore kara Shuyaku

00:22:59.292 --> 00:23:01.661
So, let's begin...
Henshin Byouyomi o Shite yo!

00:23:01.661 --> 00:23:05.495
...the countdown for the change!
Henshin Byouyomi o Shite yo!

00:23:08.968 --> 00:23:11.766
Take a deep breath, and one two.
12345 Ikizugi o One Two

00:23:12.905 --> 00:23:15.241
Now stride out...
Saa Kore kara Kuridasou

00:23:15.241 --> 00:23:18.404
...with your head held high.
Saa Kore kara Kuridasou

00:23:18.544 --> 00:23:22.275
Downtown Dance
